---
import ContentSection from "~/components/content-section.astro";
---

<ContentSection title="View cut on real stock" id="intro">
  <Fragment slot="lead">
    camNC overlays your programmed toolpath on a live camera feed so you can double-check stock orientation, offsets, and clearance before the spindle spins up.
  </Fragment>
  <div class="flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-4 text-center text-default">
    <p>
      Position an overhead camera, walk through the calibration steps, and the overlay locks itself to the machine coordinates. From then on you can
      glance at the screen to confirm the cut will land where you expect or spot clamps that need to move.
    </p>
    <p>
      Snap-to-toolpath and drag-to-zero interactions keep setup effortless, while hide-machine mode prevents the gantry from blocking your view of the stock.
    </p>
  </div>

</ContentSection>
